CAT = "hkle1Exchanges"; SEG = "EXC"
Q = [
("Shares traded on the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong are generally settled through CCASS on:",
 "T+2", ["T+0", "T+1", "T+30"],
 "On-exchange trades between participants settle in CCASS, operated by HKSCC, on the second settlement day after the trade."),
("During the Stock Exchange's continuous trading session, which order type matches only at its specified price?",
 "Limit order", ["At-auction order", "Enhanced limit order", "Special limit order"],
 "A limit order matches only at its specified price. An enhanced limit order can match up to ten price levels at once, a special limit order the same but its balance is cancelled, and at-auction orders are for the auctions."),
("At-auction orders on the Stock Exchange can be entered:",
 "In the auction sessions", ["Only during continuous trading", "Only after the market closes", "Only on half-trading days"],
 "At-auction and at-auction limit orders are used in the pre-opening session and the closing auction session, where a single price is set for matching."),
("A Stock Exchange participant must be:",
 "A Type 1 licensed corporation", ["An authorized bank", "A listed company", "A licensed insurer"],
 "To trade on the Stock Exchange a firm must be an Exchange Participant, which requires being a licensed corporation for Type 1 dealing in securities."),
("Under the Stock Exchange's short selling rules, a short sale order generally may not be placed:",
 "Below the best ask price", ["Above the day's high", "In a designated security", "On a half-trading day"],
 "The tick rule bars short selling below the best current ask price, and short sales are allowed only in designated securities."),
("When the Volatility Control Mechanism is triggered for a stock, trading:",
 "Stays in a price band for 5 minutes", ["Stops for the rest of the day", "Moves to the closing auction", "Is cancelled and reversed"],
 "The VCM starts a 5-minute cooling-off period during which trading continues only within a fixed price band, then normal trading resumes."),
("A stock option holder exercises a call option on the Stock Exchange. The holder will:",
 "Buy at the strike price", ["Sell the shares at the strike", "Receive the option premium", "Pay only the margin"],
 "A call gives the holder the right to buy the underlying shares at the strike price. The writer receives the premium and must deliver the shares if assigned."),
("Which party to a stock option must post margin?",
 "The option writer", ["The option holder", "Both parties equally", "Neither party"],
 "The writer has an obligation to perform if assigned, so must provide margin. The holder pays the premium in full and has no further obligation."),
("Futures positions on the Futures Exchange are marked to market:",
 "Daily", ["Monthly", "Only at expiry", "Only when closed"],
 "Gains and losses are settled daily through variation margin, so losses cannot build up unpaid until expiry."),
("A client must report a large open position in Hang Seng Index futures because it exceeds:",
 "The reportable level", ["The prescribed limit for margin", "The tick size rule", "The board lot size"],
 "Under the Contracts Limits and Reportable Positions Rules, a person holding a position above the reportable level must report it, and nobody may exceed the prescribed position limit without authorisation."),
("Under Stock Connect, Hong Kong and overseas investors buy eligible Mainland A shares through:",
 "Northbound trading", ["Southbound trading", "The Futures Exchange", "An IPO subscription only"],
 "Northbound trading lets investors trade eligible Shanghai and Shenzhen shares through Hong Kong brokers; southbound lets Mainland investors trade eligible Hong Kong shares."),
("Under Stock Connect northbound trading, an investor who buys A shares in the morning:",
 "Cannot sell them the same day", ["Must sell them that day", "Can sell them in the afternoon", "Must hold them a full year"],
 "Northbound A shares settle on T+0 for securities, but day trading is not allowed: shares bought today can be sold only from the next trading day."),
("A derivative warrant issuer listing on the Stock Exchange must appoint:",
 "A liquidity provider", ["A takeover adviser", "An MPF trustee", "A share registrar abroad"],
 "Issuers of listed structured products, such as derivative warrants and CBBCs, must appoint a liquidity provider to quote prices on the Stock Exchange."),
("A callable bull/bear contract (CBBC) is terminated early when:",
 "The underlying hits the call price", ["The issuer wants to raise new funds", "Trading volume falls", "The holder asks for it"],
 "A mandatory call event happens when the underlying asset's price reaches the call price, and the CBBC is called and stops trading."),
("When marketing listed structured products to the public, a firm must ensure its materials:",
 "Are fair and balanced", ["Promise a fixed return", "Omit the issuer's name", "Avoid any risk warning"],
 "Marketing of listed structured products must be fair, accurate and balanced, stating the key risks, including that the products are not principal protected."),
("Which HKEX subsidiary acts as the central counterparty for futures traded on the Futures Exchange?",
 "HKCC", ["HKSCC", "SEOCH", "SEHK"],
 "HKFE Clearing Corporation (HKCC) clears and guarantees futures and options traded on the Futures Exchange. HKSCC clears shares."),
]
